{"id":3067,"date":"2024-11-25T10:31:45","date_gmt":"2024-11-25T02:31:45","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/?post_type=product&#038;p=3067"},"modified":"2024-12-01T11:16:45","modified_gmt":"2024-12-01T03:16:45","slug":"ptfe-filter-bags","status":"publish","type":"product","link":"https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/?product=ptfe-filter-bags","title":{"rendered":"PTFE Filter Bags"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"product-post\" data-elementor-id=\"3067\" class=\"elementor elementor-3067\" data-elementor-post-type=\"product\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5356333 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"5356333\" data-element_type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-65639f1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"65639f1\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"536\" src=\"https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/11\/Wholesale-PTFE-Filter-Bags-\u8be6\u60c51-1024x536.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-3072\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/11\/Wholesale-PTFE-Filter-Bags-\u8be6\u60c51-1024x536.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/11\/Wholesale-PTFE-Filter-Bags-\u8be6\u60c51-300x157.jpg 300w, https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/11\/Wholesale-PTFE-Filter-Bags-\u8be6\u60c51-768x402.jpg 768w, https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/11\/Wholesale-PTFE-Filter-Bags-\u8be6\u60c51-600x314.jpg 600w, https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/11\/Wholesale-PTFE-Filter-Bags-\u8be6\u60c51.jpg 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-cf7edab elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"cf7edab\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>PTFE (polytetrafluoroethylene), also known as Teflon, is a polymer material with excellent properties. This material is resistant to acids, alkalis, and various organic solvents, and is almost insoluble in all solvents. It is also resistant to high temperatures and has an extremely low friction coefficient.<\/p><hr \/><h3>Feature of PTFE Filter Bags<\/h3><ul><li><strong>Excellent high temperature resistance<\/strong>: Withstands continuous operating temperatures up to 260\u00b0C (500\u00b0F) and can reach up to 300\u00b0C (572\u00b0F).<\/li><li><strong>Excellent acid and alkali resistance<\/strong>: PTFE can withstand almost all chemicals, making it an ideal material for filtering corrosive substances.<\/li><li><strong>High filtration efficiency<\/strong>: Low coefficient of friction helps prevent particles from sticking and effectively captures fine particles.<\/li><li><strong>Hydrophobicity<\/strong>: PTFE naturally repels water and other liquids, helping to control humidity in critical applications<\/li><li><strong>Durable<\/strong>: The service life can reach 6 years under normal operating conditions in the temperature range of 66\u00b0C to 204\u00b0C.<\/li><\/ul><hr \/><h3>Filtration Principle of PTFE Filter Bags<\/h3><ul><li><strong>Physical filtration<\/strong>: PTFE filter bag filters particles with its microporous structure, and its pore size is usually between 0.1 micron and 1 micron. When gas or liquid passes through the filter bag, larger particles will be blocked by the pore size of the filter bag, while smaller particles can pass through the pore size of the filter bag, thus achieving the purpose of filtration.<\/li><li><strong>Surface filtration<\/strong>: Its porous surface can capture and aggregate particles to form a dense filter layer to prevent smaller particles from passing through. When the filter layer formed in the early stage is thick enough, its filtration effect will be better.<\/li><li><strong>Inertial interception<\/strong>: Inertial interception refers to the inertia of particles in gas or liquid that prevents them from directly passing through the pore size of the filter bag and being intercepted. When particles flow through the filter bag, the inertial force will cause larger and heavier particles to deviate from the direction of the airflow and be intercepted on the surface of the filter bag.<\/li><li><strong>Electrostatic adsorption<\/strong>: Due to the charged nature of the surface of the PTFE filter bag, when there are charged fine particles in the gas, they will be adsorbed by the static electricity on the surface of the filter bag, thereby increasing the filtration effect.<\/li><\/ul><hr \/><h3>Physical Properties<\/h3><table width=\"100%\"><tbody><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">Air permeability(L\/m\u00b2.s) @200pa<\/td><td colspan=\"2\">Tensile strength(N\/5 cm)<\/td><td colspan=\"2\">Temperature(\u2103 \/ \u2109)<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>warp<\/td><td>weft<\/td><td>Operating<\/td><td>Ultimate<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>100~200<\/td><td>1000<\/td><td>1100<\/td><td>260 \/ 500<\/td><td>300 \/ 572<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><h3>Chemical Properties<\/h3><table width=\"100%\"><tbody><tr><td>Acid Resistance<\/td><td>Alkali Resistance<\/td><td>Hydrolytic Resistance<\/td><td>Oxidation Resistance<\/td><td>Abrasion resistance<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Excellent<\/td><td>Excellent<\/td><td>Excellent<\/td><td>Excellent<\/td><td>Moderate<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><h3>Specifications<\/h3><table width=\"681\"><tbody><tr><td width=\"72\">Heat resistance<\/td><td width=\"72\">Up to 300\u2103<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Fabric<\/td><td>100% PTFE fiber<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Length &amp; diameter<\/td><td>No limited<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Thickness<\/td><td>1.0-1.8mm<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Air permeability<\/td><td>30-80mm<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Area weight (g\/m\u00b2)<\/td><td>700~800<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Working lifetime<\/td><td>12000 hours and more<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Breaking elongation (%)<\/td><td>(Warp): &lt;40<br \/>(Weft): &lt;60<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Breaking strength<\/td><td>(Warp): &gt;1350<br \/>(Weft): &gt;1450<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><h3>Surface Treatment of PTFE Filter Bags<\/h3><p>There are 2 kinds of treatment : \u201cPTFE film\u201d and \u201cPTFE dipping\u201d<\/p><ul><li><strong>PTFE film:<\/strong>\u00a0Improve filtration precision: \u226410mg\/m\u00b3, but lower the filtration efficiency; and a substantial increase in acid-base resistance property.<\/li><li><strong>PTFE dipping:<\/strong>\u00a0Improve filtration precision: \u226425mg\/m\u00b3, does not lower the filtration efficiency; and a small increase in acid-base resistance property.<\/li><\/ul><hr \/><h3>Applications<\/h3><p>PTFE filter bags can provide excellent filtering effects in various harsh filtering environments. The application of this material not only improves the filtering efficiency, but also brings more possibilities to industrial production and promotes the progress and development of the industry.<\/p><ul><li><strong>Chemical Processing<\/strong>: Used in environments where aggressive chemicals are handled.<\/li><li><strong>Pharmaceuticals<\/strong>: Ensures product purity and compliance with stringent industry standards.<\/li><li><strong>Food and Beverage<\/strong>: Maintains high standards of hygiene and product quality.<\/li><li><strong>Mining and Metals<\/strong>: Effective in dust collection systems where high temperatures and corrosive gases are present.<\/li><li><strong>Waste Incineration<\/strong>: Withstands high temperatures and corrosive gases produced during incineration.<\/li><li><strong>Cement Plants<\/strong>: Used in kiln and mill processes where temperatures are high.<\/li><\/ul>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c5f56